{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mq8zin6e3bt","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Gated-classifier benchmark: harness ready, blocked only on Bash execution","summary":"\"Redo benchmarks with classifier in place\" means re-run the held-out A/B (scripts/bench-heldout.js) with --consult=gated — the GATE-FIRST path where lib/context-gate.js (the abstain-by-default INJECT/ABSTAIN classifier) decides retrieval per task — replacing the FORCED --consult=search used in the prior run (bench/heldout/results-heldout.json, generated 2026-06-10). The classifier hypothesis to prove: gate STILL fires on the winnable cases (task-transcript, locale-sum → preserve cold 0/10 → warm ~8.8/10 win) AND ABSTAINS on self-solvable cases (sum-basic/native-store/etc → avoid the over-deliberation tax that made every forced-ON arm in v1-v7 flounder MORE). Harness is fully built: PREAMBLE.gated in bench-heldout.js, Phase 2 candidates sum-basic/overlay-save/bench-metric registered with specs+graders under bench/heldout/, gate validated offline by test/context-gate-regression.test.js (recall 1.0 / precision 1.0 on the n=9 calibration set). RUN COMMAND per cell: node scripts/bench-heldout.js --candidate <name> --arm on --trial <t> --consult=gated (+ matching --arm off baselines), then aggregate. BLOCKER: this worker session has Bash hard-denied (sandbox), so the headless `claude -p` subprocesses + node graders cannot execute. Re-dispatch in a session with Bash enabled; nothing else is missing.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-11T04:15:36.662Z","vec":[-0.08254824578762054,-0.023365534842014313,-0.062013499438762665,0.06368780136108398,0.015086689032614231,-0.028003258630633354,-0.030002156272530556,0.012738066725432873,-0.020981742069125175,0.009297432377934456,-0.06047039106488228,-0.019507471472024918,0.010154970921576023,-0.044228557497262955,0.010996886529028416,-0.014473136514425278,0.07854290306568146,-0.028824076056480408,-0.06986015290021896,-0.08725655823945999,0.04072